          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Molten lead bromide, PbBr<sub>2</sub>(l), is electrolysed using a current of 2.40 A for 12.0 minutes.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 2
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bromine gas, Br<sub>2</sub>(g), is produced at the anode.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "parts": [
          {
            "key": "b.i",
            "label": "(i)",
            "type": "calculation",
            "marks": 2,
            "source": {
              "qp": 2,
              "ms": 7
            },
            "stem": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Calculate the amount, in mol, of Br<sub>2</sub>(g) produced."
              },
              {
                "type": "answerLines",
                "labels": [
                  "amount of Br<sub>2</sub>(g) = ........ mol"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "topics": [
              {
                "ref": "24.1(3)",
                "role": "primary"
              }
            ],
            "markScheme": {
              "marks": 2,
              "instruction": null,
              "guidance": [
                "<b>A</b> 0.00896 or 0.008955.",
                "1.4945 × 10<sup>–4</sup> (no × 60) [1].",
                "0.0179 [1] (no ÷ 2).",
                "Correct answer [2].",
                "0.009 [1] (1sf)."
              ],
              "points": [
                {
                  "n": 1,
                  "text": "<b>M1</b> 2.4 × 12 × 60 <b>or 1728</b> (C)",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 2,
                  "text": "<b>M2</b> 1728 / (2 × 96 500) = <b>0.00895 / 0.0090</b> mol min 2sf",
                  "numberedInMs": false,
                  "alternatives": [
                    "1728 / (2 × (1.6 × 10<sup>–19</sup> × 6.022 × 10<sup>23</sup>)) = 0.00897 min 2sf ecf"
                  ],
                  "alternativeJoin": "or"
                }
              ],
              "source": {
                "ms": 7
              }
            },
            "er": [],
            "aiSupplement": {
              "explanation": [
                {
                  "text": "First find the charge passed with <i>Q</i> = <i>It</i>, using the time in seconds: 2.40 × 12.0 × 60 = 1728 C. Then use the Faraday constant to change charge into moles of electrons: 1728 / 96 500 = 0.0179 mol e<sup>–</sup>. At the anode 2Br<sup>–</sup> → Br<sub>2</sub> + 2e<sup>–</sup>, so two moles of electrons give one mole of Br<sub>2</sub>: 0.0179 / 2 = 0.00895 mol.",
                  "refs": [
                    "ms:b.i#1",
                    "ms:b.i#2",
                    "syllabus:24.1(3)"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "The MS also accepts building <i>F</i> from <i>F</i> = <i>Le</i> (1.6 × 10<sup>–19</sup> × 6.022 × 10<sup>23</sup>), which gives 0.00897 mol because of rounding in <i>e</i>.",
                  "refs": [
                    "ms:b.i#2",
                    "syllabus:24.1(2)"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reasoningChain": [
                "Convert the time: 12.0 min × 60 = 720 s.",
                "Q = It = 2.40 × 720 = 1728 C.",
                "Moles of electrons = 1728 / 96 500 = 0.0179 mol.",
                "2Br⁻ → Br₂ + 2e⁻, so n(Br₂) = 0.0179 / 2 = 0.00895 mol."
              ],
              "inferredMistakes": [
                {
                  "text": "Leaving the time in minutes, which gives 1.4945 × 10⁻⁴ mol and only [1].",
                  "basis": "inferred",
                  "refs": [
                    "ms:b.i#1"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Forgetting that 2 mol of electrons are needed per mole of Br₂, which gives 0.0179 and only [1].",
                  "basis": "inferred",
                  "refs": [
                    "ms:b.i#2"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Rounding the answer to 0.009 (1 sf), which loses a mark.",
                  "basis": "inferred",
                  "refs": [
                    "ms:b.i#2"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
