                {
                  "text": "The amount of Br<sub>2</sub> comes from 1(b)(i), so the mark is given ecf on that value. Br<sub>2</sub> boils at about 59 °C, so at 380 °C it is a gas and the ideal gas equation applies.",
                  "refs": [
                    "ms:b.ii#1",
                    "syllabus:24.1(3)"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reasoningChain": [
                "Convert units: p = 101 000 Pa, T = 653 K.",
                "V = nRT / p = 0.00895 × 8.31 × 653 / 101 000 = 4.81 × 10⁻⁴ m³.",
                "Convert to dm³: × 1000 = 0.481 dm³ (3 sf)."
