            {
              "n": 5,
              "text": "<b>M2</b> ans ÷ 1.6 × 10<sup>–19</sup> = <b>6.08 × 10<sup>23</sup></b> <b>must be 3sf</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            }
          ],
          "source": {
            "ms": 8
          }
        },
        "er": [],
        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "At the cathode Na<sup>+</sup> + e<sup>–</sup> → Na, so one electron is needed for each sodium atom. Two counts are compared. The number of electrons passed is the charge divided by the charge on one electron: 36 000 / 1.6 × 10<sup>–19</sup> = 2.25 × 10<sup>23</sup>. The number of moles of sodium is 8.51 / 23.0 = 0.370 mol. Since 0.370 mol of Na contains 2.25 × 10<sup>23</sup> atoms, one mole contains 2.25 × 10<sup>23</sup> / 0.370 = 6.08 × 10<sup>23</sup>, which is <i>L</i>.",
              "refs": [
                "ms:c#1",
                "ms:c#2",
                "ms:c#3",
                "syllabus:24.1(4)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "The second route uses <i>F</i> = <i>Le</i>: the charge per mole of electrons is 36 000 / 0.370 = 97 297 C mol<sup>–1</sup>, and dividing by <i>e</i> gives the same <i>L</i>. The answer must be given to 3 sf; 6 × 10<sup>23</sup> or 6.1 × 10<sup>23</sup> does not score.",
              "refs": [
                "ms:c#4",
                "ms:c#5",
                "syllabus:24.1(2)"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Electrons passed = Q / e = 36 000 / 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 2.25 × 10²³.",
            "Moles of Na = 8.51 / 23.0 = 0.370 mol (1 e⁻ per Na⁺).",
            "L = 2.25 × 10²³ / 0.370 = 6.08 × 10²³ mol⁻¹ (3 sf)."
          ],
